                    "urls": [],
                    "user_mentions": [
                      {
                        "id_str": "2064735918867484672",
                        "indices": [
                          152,
                          165
                        ],
                        "name": "Good Enough",
                        "screen_name": "GoodEnoughAi"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "id": "Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwODgzMTg4MTQ0MjUzNTgzMzc=",
                  "media": {
                    "inline_media": []
                  },
                  "richtext": {
                    "richtext_tags": []
                  },
                  "text": "I built a LinkedIn scraper this afternoon that finds our next 1,000 waitlist signups. Total cost: about $5/month.\n\nHere's the playbook we're running at @GoodEnoughAi.\n\nWhen Google shipped Gemini 3.7 Flash yesterday, the entire comment section under the launch posts was engineers talking about one thing: better AND cheaper. Those people are our exact customers. We sell managed open-source models at 70-90% less than frontier pricing. Someone reacting to a \"cheaper model\" post is raising their hand in public.\n\nSo instead of buying lead lists, we scrape the hands.\n\nThe stack:\n→ Apify no-cookie actors scrape reactions + comments off any LinkedIn post ($2 per 1,000 people, zero account risk, no burner logins)\n→ Apollo enriches each profile URL into title, company, headcount\n→ A scoring pass filters for our ICP: US builders, heads of AI, data eng leads, agencies\n→ Top matches get a human look, the rest flow into outreach\n→ Everything lands in our Notion, nothing sends without approval\n\nBuilt the whole thing with Claude Code in one session. First run pulled 217 people off a single post. Today's batch is 7 posts (the Gemini 3.7 launch wave plus open-model releases) for about 1,000 prospects, at a cost of roughly $2.\n\nOne rule we learned the hard way: only scrape posts under a month old. We pulled a 2024 post first and got 200 people whose \"intent\" was two years stale: fresh engagement or nothing.\n\nDistribution isn't about reach; it's about finding the people already telling the market they want what you sell.\n\nDM \"scrape\" and i'll shoot over the entire strategy."
                }
              }
